panasonic-cf19 (1.4.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * panasonic-hbtn: support the Toughpad FZ-G1 (ACPI device MAT002A/MAT002B):
    its two bezel buttons A1 (HINF codes 0x38/0x39) and A2 (0x42/0x43) are
    reported as KEY_PROG1 and KEY_PROG2 taps.  No tablet-mode switch is
    reported for it.
  * DKMS: build only for kernels 6.12 and newer (BUILD_EXCLUSIVE_KERNEL); an
    older kernel with incomplete headers made the package fail to configure.
  * The rotation and "security" buttons of the CF-19 are now named in a
    convertible-helper profile (profiles/panasonic-cf19.conf), because
    convertible-helper 1.2.0 no longer acts on those keys on other machines.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 19:00:00 -0700

panasonic-cf19 (1.3.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Move everything that does not need the GNOME Shell out of the extension
    into the new package convertible-helper (a user service using only evdev
    events and mutter's DisplayConfig D-Bus API): the rotation button and
    the "security" button, and the on-screen keyboard setting in tablet
    mode.  The extension now only shows and hides the keyboard.
  * panasonic-hbtn: the rotation button now sends KEY_PROG3 (XF86Launch3),
    which GNOME does not bind, so convertible-helper is its only handler.
  * panasonic-cf19-support depends on convertible-helper.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 15:00:00 -0700

panasonic-cf19 (1.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * panasonic-cf19-support: the GNOME Shell extension now handles the rotation
    button itself (new schema key "rotate"), so it works while a dialog or menu
    is open.  GNOME's own rotate-monitor shortcut is switched off while the
    extension runs and restored when it is disabled.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 12:30:00 -0700

panasonic-cf19 (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * panasonic-cf19-support: replace the libinput calibration rule by a relay
    service (cf19-touch-relay) that reads the touch panel, applies the same
    calibration and re-emits it as a touchscreen device.  GNOME treated the
    panel as a pointer and did not rotate its mapping with the display; the
    touchscreen device is rotated.  Needs python3.  Reboot (or re-plug the
    panel) after installing.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Wed, 28 Oct 2026 11:10:00 -0700

panasonic-cf19 (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release: Panasonic Toughbook CF-19 support for Debian 13 (trixie)
    with GNOME 48, verified on a CF-19 Mk5 (CF-19AHUAX1M).
  * panasonic-hbtn-dkms: tablet button driver for kernel 6.12 (rework of the
    2012 panasonic-hbtn driver); adds the SW_TABLET_MODE switch for the swivel
    screen and the tablet_mode sysfs attribute.
  * panasonic-cf19-support: touch screen calibration (udev), GNOME Shell
    extension for the keyboard and "security" buttons (with its own
    GSettings schema and a default that enables it), speaker fix for
    PipeWire's mixer path.

 -- Bruce Perens <bruce@perens.com>  Tue, 27 Oct 2026 19:52:15 -0700
